sfwbar for FlickOS
==================

Upstream: https://github.com/LBCrion/sfwbar (GPL-3). Debian trixie doesn't
have it (Debian's package stopped at 1.0~beta13 and was removed), so FlickOS
packages it natively. It is the only compiled FlickOS package
(Architecture: any, built with meson by debian/rules).

This folder is upstream's source tree at git commit d40912d (main,
2026-09-10), without .github/, packaging/, .gitattributes and
doc/sfwbar.rst.bak.

Changes to upstream (marked "FlickOS:" in the code):
  - src/gui/taskbarpopup.c: taskbar_popup_update() sets the CSS class
    "running" on an app's button while it has a window, not only its pin.
    flickos-layouts' Cupertino dock.css draws the open-app line with it.
  - src/gui/bar.c, bar.h: bar property sensor_maximized (boolean). With a
    sensor, the bar stays shown and hides only while the focused window is
    maximized or fullscreen on the bar's output (bar_may_hide). A window
    listener re-checks all bars after window changes. Not in the man pages
    (doc/ isn't rebuilt).
  - src/ipc/foreign-toplevel.c: toplevel_handle_state() calls
    wintree_commit(), so listeners hear about state changes such as
    maximizing (upstream only notified them on focus changes).
  - src/workspace.c: workspace_mod_state() compares only the flags it
    changes. Upstream compared all state flags, so once one was set (every
    shown workspace is "visible") no other could be, and the pager never
    marked the active workspace "focused" (seen with labwc's ext-workspace).
    flickos-layouts' Traditional desktop switcher highlights it.
  - src/gui/bar.c: no longer forces gtk-enable-animations on, so a bar
    follows GSettings' enable-animations (FlickOS's Settings >
    Accessibility > Animations). bar_sensor_hide() finishes the hide at
    once when the revealer hid without an animation: upstream connected
    its notify::child-revealed handler after the revealer had already
    notified, so the sensor never came back (the reason, it seems, for
    forcing animations on; transition = 0 hit it too).
  - src/lib/compositor.c: WindowInfo() takes a taskbar group button's
    window (group = popup) from the action, as Focus() and Minimize() do.
    Upstream read the group's app id as a window_t, so
    WindowInfo('focused') was false and a click on the Cupertino dock never
    minimized the focused app (TaskbarItemDefault).
  - src/sfwbar.c: activate() starts the scanner thread after expr_init()
    and scanner_init(), as upstream does since 88c83b9. Started before
    them, the thread's first scanner_invalidate() could lock the still
    NULL scan_list: a segfault at address 8 in thread "scanner" now and
    then at start, seen when a layout switch started the dock. Drop this
    entry when updating past 88c83b9.
  - src/gui/bar.c: bar_resize() asks for no length for a full-length bar
    (anchored to both ends), so it takes the length the compositor gives
    it. Upstream asked for the monitor's length, so the Footprint layout's
    left dock, below the top bar's exclusive zone, ran 30 px past the
    bottom of the screen and cut off its Show Apps button.

Why a git commit and not a release: the latest release, 1.0_beta17, lacks
taskbar pins (documented but only implemented for the pager) and its
size = "auto" bars collapse to 1px. Both work in d40912d. Switch to the
first release after beta17 once it is out.

Updating to upstream commit or release REF:

  1. git clone https://github.com/LBCrion/sfwbar && cd sfwbar
  2. Replace everything here except debian/ with
     git archive REF | tar -x --exclude=.github --exclude=packaging \
         --exclude=.gitattributes --exclude=doc/sfwbar.rst.bak
  3. Make the changes above again (git diff d40912d before replacing shows
     them).
  4. Compare meson.build's dependency() lines and meson_options.txt with
     debian/control's Build-Depends and debian/rules' feature options.
  5. Update the commit above, and debian/copyright if protocols/ changed.
  6. dch -v VERSION -D trixie "New upstream ...", with VERSION
     1.0~betaN+flickos1 for a release, or 1.0~betaN+gitYYYYMMDD+flickos1
     for a commit after release N.
